koha (26.06.00~1) unstable; urgency=medium

  New Koha installations use SQL polling for background job notifications.
  RabbitMQ is now suggested rather than required by koha-common and
  koha-deps, so it is not installed automatically with these packages.

  Existing JobsNotificationMethod settings are preserved. Sites already
  using STOMP continue to use their configured broker. Koha's maintainer
  scripts do not remove or stop RabbitMQ. Koha package upgrades configure
  and restart a local RabbitMQ broker only when an instance uses STOMP
  with a local broker hostname.

  If RabbitMQ was installed automatically as a dependency and you still
  need it, mark it as manually installed before using apt autoremove:

    apt-mark manual rabbitmq-server

  To switch an existing instance to polling, change JobsNotificationMethod
  and restart its background workers. The workers remain necessary in both
  modes. Polling checks for new jobs every ten seconds. Before stopping or
  removing RabbitMQ, check all Koha instances and other broker users.

  To use STOMP on a new installation, install and configure a local broker
  or configure a remote broker, enable its STOMP support, select STOMP in
  JobsNotificationMethod and restart the background workers. See the
  background job section of README.Debian for details.

 -- Koha Development Team <koha-devel@lists.koha-community.org>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0000
